From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xwm: retain the requested session refresh rate for Steam UI

A 120 Hz session on a 144 Hz panel was switched to the panel maximum as
soon as Steam mapped its UI, despite Xwayland still advertising 120 Hz.
Keep a supported requested rate for the UI and retain game-specific rates.

--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -3767,9 +3767,15 @@
 
 		int nDynamicRefreshHz = g_nDynamicRefreshRate[GetBackend()->GetScreenType()];
 
+		// Keep Steam at the session's requested refresh rate instead of
+		// immediately replacing -r with the panel maximum. The Xwayland
+		// output also uses this rate, so UI presentation stays in cadence.
+		int nSteamRefreshHz = gamescope::ConvertmHzToHz( g_nNestedRefresh );
+		if ( std::find( rates.begin(), rates.end(), nSteamRefreshHz ) == rates.end() )
+			nSteamRefreshHz = int( rates.back() );
 		int nTargetRefreshHz = nDynamicRefreshHz && steamcompmgr_window_should_refresh_switch( pFocus->focusWindow )
 			? nDynamicRefreshHz
-			: int( rates[ rates.size() - 1 ] );
+			: nSteamRefreshHz;
 
 		uint64_t now = get_time_in_nanos();
 
